-- S23 Maharashtra prose — ozar
-- Verdict matrix: 8 go / 1 skip / 3 wait
-- Anchors: Vighneshwar — 5th Ashtavinayak in yatra order, remover-of-obstacles form, Kukdi river bank, sone-Ganesh (gold-leaf-coated murti), 1785 renovation by Chimaji Appa post-Vasai victory over Portuguese (Bajirao I's brother), original temple destroyed in earlier raids, Pune 85km via Chakan-Junnar, near Lenyadri 10km

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('ozar', 1, 'go', 4, 'January at Ozar — the fifth temple in the traditional Ashtavinayak yatra — runs at clean post-festival operational tempo. Vighneshwar (the remover-of-obstacles form of Ganesha) sits on the Kukdi river bank 85km north of Pune via Chakan and Junnar. The murti is sone-Ganesh (gold-leaf coated); the present structure dates to the 1785 renovation commissioned by Chimaji Appa (Peshwa Bajirao I''s younger brother) following his Vasai victory over the Portuguese — the original temple had been destroyed in earlier Mughal-era raids. The temple complex sits in the Junnar valley with the Manmodi hills (housing Lenyadri 10km away) on the northern horizon. Daytime 14-28C, nights 8-10C — among the cleanest temple weather of the year. The 85km Pune drive takes 2 hours via Chakan-Manchar-Narayangaon-Junnar. Combine with Lenyadri 10km in the same morning. Sankashti Chaturthi early month brings Tuesday density. Kukdi river at clean post-monsoon flow visible from the temple ghat.', 'January 14-28C clean weather. Sone-Ganesh (gold-leaf) Vighneshwar 1785 Chimaji Appa structure on Kukdi river. 85km Pune drive 2 hours via Chakan-Junnar. Combine with Lenyadri 10km. Sankashti Tuesday flow.', NULL),
('ozar', 2, 'go', 5, 'February at Ozar makes Maghi Ganesh Jayanti a peak event. The festival — Magh Shukla Chaturthi — falls Wednesday 4 February 2026. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar murti (the gold-leaf-coated form, distinctive among the eight Ashtavinayak) receives the pre-dawn maha-abhishek ritual from 4am; palki processions run morning and evening; the 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone structure handles festival crowd density without strain. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 3 February 2026 compounding pilgrim density. Daytime 16-30C, nights 10-12C — clean temple weather. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar takes 2.5 hours on festival days. Devotees combine Ozar with Lenyadri (10km away) into a single day or stay overnight at Junnar (8km) for both temples. The post-Vasai-victory historical anchor (Chimaji Appa''s 1785 renovation following his Maharashtra-Portuguese campaign) pulls heritage-pilgrim flow alongside the standard yatra. Lodgings at Junnar ₹800-2,200 festival rates. Book 2 weeks ahead.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 + Angarki Feb 3 at sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar. Pre-dawn maha-abhishek of gold-leaf murti. 1785 Chimaji Appa Vasai-victory structure. Combine with Lenyadri 10km. Junnar lodgings ₹800-2,200.', NULL),
('ozar', 3, 'go', 4, 'March at Ozar holds clean operational temperature through first three weeks. Gudi Padwa Thursday 19 March 2026 brings extended morning ritual at Vighneshwar and the wider Junnar-valley Marathi community attends. Daytime 20-33C, nights 14-16C. The sone-Ganesh murti — the gold-leaf-coated form — runs standard 5am-9:30pm darshan; the 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone interior holds light cool through the day. The Kukdi river runs at low pre-monsoon flow; the temple ghat clean. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard density. The 85km Pune drive remains 2 hours via Chakan-Junnar. Lenyadri 10km combinable in the same morning — both temples align easily on a Pune day-trip schedule. Combine optionally with Shivneri Fort at Junnar (where Shivaji was born in 1630) for a Maharashtra-heritage extension. By final week the heat ramp arrives — mid-day temple courtyard becomes uncomfortable. Lodgings ₹500-1,400. Last clean window before April compression.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 extended ritual at sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar. 20-33C first 3 weeks. Combine with Lenyadri 10km same morning + optional Shivneri Fort 8km (Shivaji birthplace 1630). Last clean window before April heat.', NULL),
('ozar', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April pushes Ozar into heat-compromise territory. Daytime 25-38C in the Junnar valley; the temple courtyard stone holds heat 8am-7pm. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar darshan compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm windows. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone interior holds cooler 33-35C — the gold-leaf coating on the murti reflects the dim cool sanctum lighting. The Kukdi river at lowest pre-monsoon flow — the riverbed mostly dry, the ghat steps dust-covered. Pilgrim arrivals thin through month; lodging rates drop to ₹400-1,000. The committed pilgrim flow attempting the Ozar-Lenyadri combination shifts to dawn-only timing. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar remains 2 hours but the temple visit itself is the failure point past 9am. Combine with Lenyadri only on confirmed pre-9am morning slots. Push to October for post-monsoon ideal window.', 'April compresses sone-Ganesh darshan to dawn and dusk. 25-38C Junnar valley. Pradakshina + ghat uncomfortable past 10am. Kukdi at lowest flow. Combine with Lenyadri pre-9am only. Push to October.', 'April runs at fragmented schedule. 25-38C heat compresses sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar darshan to dawn and dusk fragments. Kukdi river ghat dust-covered. The full Ozar-Lenyadri morning combination collapses past 9am.'),
('ozar', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is unviable Ozar. Daytime 29-41C in the Junnar valley — the Manmodi hills offer minimal heat buffer; the temple stone courtyard hits 48-50C surface noon. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar darshan continues but the practical pilgrim experience collapses — even the 5am dawn slot opens at 27C and reaches 34C by closing. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone interior holds 33-35C through day; the gold-leaf coating on the murti reflects the dim cool sanctum lighting; but the open pradakshina circuit and the Kukdi ghat approach are physically punishing. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 — dedicated pilgrim flow continues at modest density but most committed yatra-pilgrims skip Ozar through May. The 85km Pune drive remains drivable but the temple visit itself is the failure point. Lenyadri 307-step climb at year-impossible heat exposure. Lodgings drop to ₹400-1,000 deep off-season. Push to October.', NULL, 'May 29-41C — Junnar valley year-hottest stretch. Temple courtyard 48-50C surface noon. Sone-Ganesh darshan continues but pradakshina uncomfortable at any hour. Kukdi ghat dust-baked. Lenyadri 307 steps unsafe. Full temple experience collapses. Push to October.'),
('ozar', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks southwest monsoon arrival in Ozar. First-week rains break the heat — daytime 21-31C, nights 18-20C. The Kukdi river starts to swell visibly through month; by final week the ghat steps below the temple begin to flood. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar darshan continues at standard 5am-9:30pm schedule — the 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone structure sits well above the river bank — but the ghat-approach photography window closes intermittently. The Junnar valley turns green; the gold-leaf coating on the Vighneshwar murti against the freshly washed temple courtyard is among the better viewing contexts of the year. Lenyadri 10km away starts to face 307-step rain-slick caution. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar can take 2.5 hours through monsoon delays. Sankashti Chaturthi late month brings modest pilgrim flow. Pilgrim lodging at Junnar ₹500-1,300 with monsoon discount.', 'June monsoon arrival — 21-31C, Junnar valley turns green. Sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar against freshly-washed temple courtyard. Kukdi river swells. Lenyadri 307 steps rain-slick. 85km Pune drive 2.5 hours through delays.', 'June transition month — Kukdi river swells through final week, ghat-approach intermittent. Lenyadri 307 steps rain-slick. 85km Pune drive 2.5 hours; expect at least one wet darshan stretch.'),
('ozar', 7, 'wait', 3, 'July holds monsoon peak rainfall in the Junnar valley — Ozar receives 350-500mm. The Kukdi river overflows the lower ghat steps reliably; the temple platform remains dry (the 1785 Chimaji-Appa structure sits well above the riverbed) but the ghat approach becomes unusable on heavy-rain days. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar darshan continues at reduced morning-only schedule on monsoon days. The gold-leaf-coated murti in the cool stone interior against the lush Manmodi-hills monsoon-green setting is visually striking. Lenyadri 10km is physically dangerous through July — 307 wet basalt steps hold zero grip. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar takes 2.5-3 hours through caution sections. AC-bus packages drop to ₹450-700 day-trip rates. Sankashti Chaturthi pilgrim flow modest. Lodgings at Junnar drop to ₹400-1,200 deep monsoon rates. Time the visit to morning windows after overnight rain has cleared.', 'July sone-Ganesh against monsoon-green Manmodi hills visually striking. Kukdi river overflows lower ghat. 85km Pune drive 2.5-3 hours. AC-bus ₹450-700. Morning-only reliable. Lenyadri 307 steps unsafe.', 'July monsoon peak — Kukdi river overflows lower ghat through month. Lenyadri 10km combination unsafe (307 wet basalt steps). AC-bus services on weather-watch suspension. The reliable yatra experience does not happen.'),
('ozar', 8, 'wait', 3, 'August continues monsoon peak with Angarki Chaturthi anchor. The Tuesday-Sankashti combination falls Tuesday 4 August 2026 drawing committed pilgrim flow despite the rain. Ozar at extended ritual schedule for the festival; the sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar maha-abhishek runs pre-dawn. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa structure handles the festival density. Daytime 21-30C, humid; rainfall sustained at 300-450mm. The Kukdi river still overflows the lower ghat. Lenyadri 10km remains rain-slick — most pilgrims skip the 307-step climb and focus on Ozar alone. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar takes 2.5 hours through caution sections. Pilgrim density picks up through final week as the September Ganesh Chaturthi build approaches. Lodgings at Junnar rise to ₹500-1,400 from early-month discount.', 'Angarki Chaturthi Tue Aug 4 — sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar extended ritual despite rain. 1785 Chimaji-Appa structure handles density. 85km Pune drive 2.5 hours. Lenyadri 10km combination skipped — focus on Ozar alone.', 'August monsoon — Kukdi still overflows lower ghat, Lenyadri 10km combination unsafe. The full Ozar-Lenyadri-paired yatra collapses to Ozar-alone visits. AC-bus services on weather watch.'),
('ozar', 9, 'go', 5, 'September makes Ozar a Ganesh Chaturthi anchor. The festival (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar (the gold-leaf-coated murti — distinctive among the eight Ashtavinayak) receives continuous palki processions, special pre-dawn maha-abhishek every morning, full puran-poli and ukadiche-modak prasad distribution. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa structure runs at festival saturation. Daytime 22-30C with monsoon tail rains tapering through first week. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar takes 3-3.5 hours through festival traffic; private operators run 3-day Ashtavinayak packages including Ozar and Lenyadri Day 2. Lodgings at Junnar book 90 days ahead at ₹1,500-3,500 festival rates. The Kukdi river runs at clean late-monsoon flow with the ghat approach restored mid-month. Lenyadri 10km combination restored.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 — sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar at festival saturation. Continuous palki processions, pre-dawn maha-abhishek of gold-leaf murti. 1785 Chimaji-Appa structure. Junnar lodgings ₹1,500-3,500. Lenyadri 10km combination restored.', NULL),
('ozar', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is post-monsoon ideal Ozar. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed; through first two weeks the residue continues at strong tempo, then settles into clean operational tempo. Daytime 18-31C, nights 15-17C. Kukdi river at full post-monsoon flow; the temple ghat platform fully restored, the river running clear at clean photographic angle from the courtyard. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar murti — the gold-leaf coating reflecting the soft post-monsoon light through the temple entrance — sits in cleanest visual presentation. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone structure with the green Manmodi-hills setting at peak photographic clarity. Lenyadri 10km combination restored at year-best traction. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 bringing dedicated pilgrim density. The 85km Pune drive returns to 2-hour standard time. Lodgings ₹700-1,800. Combine with Shivneri Fort at Junnar.', 'Post-monsoon ideal — 18-31C, Kukdi river at full flow, sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar with green Manmodi backdrop. Lenyadri 10km combination restored. Angarki Tue Oct 6. Combine with Shivneri Fort at Junnar (Shivaji birthplace).', NULL),
('ozar', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Ozar. The post-monsoon Junnar-valley green holds through first two weeks; daytime 15-29C, nights 11-13C — the sharpest cool weather of the year. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar darshan at full 5am-9:30pm schedule with light woolens needed for the 5am slot. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone structure with the Manmodi-hills backdrop at cleanest visual presentation. The gold-leaf coating on the murti reflects the cool dry winter light. Kukdi river at clean post-monsoon flow; the temple ghat fully restored. Lenyadri 10km at year-best traction; the 307-step climb workable any time of day. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard density. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar runs cleanest of the year — 1h 50min on weekday mornings. Pilgrim lodgings at Junnar ₹700-1,800. Combine with Shivneri Fort 8km for Maharashtra-heritage extension.', 'November year-best — 15-29C, sharpest cool of year. Sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar + 1785 Chimaji-Appa structure at cleanest visual. Lenyadri 10km combination at year-best traction. 85km Pune drive 1h 50min. Combine with Shivneri Fort.', NULL),
('ozar', 12, 'go', 4, 'December at Ozar opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 1 December 2026, the auspicious month-opener pulling dedicated pilgrim flow. The sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar runs full ritual schedule with strong first-week density. Daytime 13-28C, nights 7-9C — year-coolest stretch; light woolens essential for 5am dawn slot, sweaters and shawls for the pre-dawn pilgrim wait. The 1785 Chimaji-Appa-era stone structure and the gold-leaf murti against the cool dry Junnar-valley setting at clean visual presentation. Kukdi river at moderate flow. The 85km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar runs heavy weekend traffic through Pune-tourist-escape season — 15 percent longer through December weekends. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard flow. Lenyadri 10km combination at full traction. Pilgrim lodgings at Junnar rise to ₹800-2,000 at year-end peak. Book mid-month weekdays for cleanest experience.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi opens strong. 13-28C year-coolest. Sone-Ganesh Vighneshwar + Lenyadri 10km combination at full traction. 85km Pune drive heavy weekend traffic. Lodgings ₹800-2,000. Mid-month weekdays cleanest.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
